inary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"missing_required_child","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct ed65's attribution of the two binding_lifecycle.py rows to child 2a95 (RP-04 C3g), which is their executable owner.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ed65 AC2: 'the only residual rows are the 2 binding_lifecycle.py entries owned by S7.3.a / 01d8-c18d-b229-419a'.","2a95 Context: 'This story is the executable drain that RP-02 S2's move left owing' and its ACs cut the binding_lifecycle grace read and remove both binding_lifecycle.py rows.","6633 file list names 'src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py' but not binding_lifecycle.py.","Ticket 01d8 is closed as 'Superseded / obsolete tracker ... executed by RP-04 C3g (ticket 2a95 ...)'; it carries no file_impact and is bookkeeping-only.","container pairing: parent + 1b07-bf4d-4aca-41c4/2a95-236b-535f-460e/6633-219e-988a-42f6/9515-ffa1-5272-4310/9e42-78f7-c164-4bc8/d074-ab22-e37a-4480/ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36"],"finding":"Child ed65 attributes the two residual binding_lifecycle.py rows to the wrong owner. It states they are 'owned by S7.3.a / 01d8-c18d-b229-419a', but the executable cut of those reads is actually child 2a95 (RP-04 C3g), and child 6633 (S7.3.a) lists binding_store.py — not binding_lifecycle.py — in its 35 files and never targets those reads.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe784b3227c485aaa","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36","norm_id":"n40058e747972f2d0","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader following ed65's attribution looks to S7.3.a (6633) to close the binding_lifecycle rows; 6633 targets binding_store.py and never touches binding_lifecycle.py, so the reader would conclude the rows are handled when the actual owner is 2a95."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Change ed65 AC2 to state the two binding_lifecycle.py rows are owned by child 2a95 (RP-04 C3g), not S7.3.a / 01d8.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm no migration switch / per-job ambient reload / migration exception remains below-seam, and assign a child to remove any that do, per parent AC3.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0929,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC3: 'Legacy facades, switches, per-job ambient reloads, and migration exceptions are removed only after their proof passes.'","Parent Context also names 'backend property reloads' and 'migration switches' as in-scope below-seam items.","Children's acceptance criteria enumerate config/credential reads and (d074/1b07/9515/ed65) read-via markers; d074 handles REBAR_SYNC_PUSH per-import env-control as owned-in-place, but no child names removal of 'migration switches' / 'per-job ambient reloads' / 'migration exceptions' as an outcome.","container pairing: parent + 1b07-bf4d-4aca-41c4/2a95-236b-535f-460e/6633-219e-988a-42f6/9515-ffa1-5272-4310/9e42-78f7-c164-4bc8/d074-ab22-e37a-4480/ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36"],"finding":"The parent AC3 items 'migration switches', 'per-job ambient reloads', and 'migration exceptions' removed only after proof are not distinctly owned by any child. Children treat only ambient config/credential reads (cut-to-seam / read-via marker / remove LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS rows); none names removal of a migration switch, a per-job ambient reload, or a migration exception as its deliverable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f68273f87953fe5fd","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"children 6633-219e-988a-42f6, d074-ab22-e37a-4480, 9515-ffa1-5272-4310, 1b07-bf4d-4aca-41c4, 9e42-78f7-c164-4bc8, ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36, 2a95-236b-535f-460e","norm_id":"n007965bc09954962","priority":0.8571,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If any migration switch, per-job ambient reload, or migration exception exists below-seam, it falls into no child's stated scope (owned-by-none), leaving a residual below-seam reload the parent AC requires removed."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Either add an explicit statement to the residual-drain child (ed65) that it also removes any migration switches / per-job ambient reloads / migration exceptions, or add a child that names those items.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"missing_required_child","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Record that 2a95's EMPTY/gate-clean assertion requires it to land last (after all six subsystem siblings), or relax its AC to a per-path membership check like ed65's.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.548,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2a95 AC3: 'LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS is now EMPTY ([]) — the whole-tree config-ownership drain is complete.'","2a95 AC4: 'python scripts/check_config_ownership.py reports zero findings with the whitelist empty.'","2a95 Context: 'After C3f (ed65) drains the nine residual files, ... LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS holds exactly TWO rows'.","ed65 acknowledges the coupling more carefully: 'The whole-tree list reaches EMPTY only once BOTH this slice and that retarget land; whichever lands last observes EMPTY.'","container pairing: parent + 1b07-bf4d-4aca-41c4/2a95-236b-535f-460e/6633-219e-988a-42f6/9515-ffa1-5272-4310/9e42-78f7-c164-4bc8/d074-ab22-e37a-4480/ed65-a3d7-1aeb-4c36"],"finding":"Child 2a95 hard-asserts LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS == [] (EMPTY, whole-tree drain complete) as its own acceptance criterion, but that outcome holds only if 2a95 lands AFTER all six subsystem siblings. Its own Context states 'After C3f (ed65) drains the nine residual files, LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS holds exactly TWO rows' — so 2a95's EMPTY assertion depends on every other sibling already having removed its rows.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8551d9343a1cd6f1","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 2a95-236b-535f-460e","norm_id":"n360a355899fe75d7","priority":0.402,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If 2a95 lands before one or more subsystem siblings (6633/d074/9515/1b07/9e42/ed65) have removed their rows, its held-out oracle asserting LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS == [] fails even though 2a95's own binding_lifecycle cut is correct."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Either add an explicit 'lands-last' ordering dependency for 2a95 on all six subsystem children, or scope its whole-tree-EMPTY assertion to 'observed EMPTY when this slice lands last' mirroring ed65's 'whichever lands last observes EMPTY' framing.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"